'''viperess''' (vī′pėr-es), ''n.'' [< ''viper'' + ''-ess.''] A female viper.
{{smaller block|Would we fain’d, but hear Pontia confess,<br>My Sons I would have poyson’d: ''Viperess!''
{{right|''Stapylton'', tr. of Juvenal (ed. 1660), vi. 670.}}}}

'''viper-fish''' (vī′pėr-fish), ''n.'' A fish of the family ''Chauliodontidæ'' and genus ''Chauliodus'', specifically ''C. sloani.'' {{smaller|This is a deep-sea fish of Mediterranean and Atlantic waters, a foot long, greenish above, blackish below, silvery on the sides, with about thirty phosphorescent spots in a row from the chin to the ventral fins.}}

